course: dictionary
lesson: 7561
title: Paying before you get it
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A prepayment is money you pay before you get something, instead of paying afterwards. The word has two parts: pre means before, and payment means money paid. So a prepayment is a payment made in advance.
explain: «A prepayment meter is paid in advance; when the money on it runs out, the electricity or gas stops until it is topped up.» The clue is paid in advance: the family pays first and then uses the energy. When the money runs out, the supply stops until more is added.
explain: «Prepayment meters often have emergency credit, and councils and charities can help families who run out often.» Here the context tells you that families can run out of money on the meter, so prepayment means paying first, and running out is a real problem that people can get help with.
fact: A prepayment is money paid before you get something.
fact: «Prepayment» can also mean paying back part of a loan early, before it is due.
fact: Pay-as-you-go phones and prepayment gas and electricity meters work this way: you top them up with money before you use them.
fact: In maths, a prepayment is taken away from the total cost to find what is left to pay.
fact: A holiday deposit is a kind of prepayment: you pay some money first, and the rest later.
exercise: «A prepayment meter is paid in advance.» What does prepayment mean? | Money paid after you have used something | Money given away for free | Money you borrow from a bank | *Money paid before you get something
exercise: A shop sign says «prepayment required». What does this tell you? | You must pay with a card only | You can pay for it next year | You get the goods for free | *You must pay before you get the goods
exercise: A total cost is 50 pounds and a prepayment of 20 pounds was made. How much is left to pay? | 50 pounds | *30 pounds | 70 pounds | 20 pounds
test: «When the money on the meter runs out, the electricity stops until it is topped up.» What does topped up mean? | Moved to a new house | Turned off for good | *Put more money on the meter | Read by a worker
test: Which of these is a prepayment? | Borrowing money from a friend | Getting a present with no money | Paying a bill a month after you use the gas | *Paying a holiday deposit before you go
exam: You pay back part of a loan early, before it is due. What is this called? | *Prepayment | Refund | Wages | Interest
